  "argument": "Records are moved fewer times between creation and execution: selection reads a record once out of its queue slot and the scheduler runs it from there, sends are written once into the queue slot, a parked record is written once into its waiting-reader entry, and a woken reader is completed in place and moved once to its local queue; frame buffers for calls and for records sent to functions that never park come from a per-run pool, and such records hold their arguments in the frame. Queue order, selection indices, eligible lists, ledger values and draw order are unchanged; no draw is added, dropped or reordered; wakes keep their semantics and error order. Executions, logs, traces and stall-cap files byte-identical at one thread on VR 3,008, crash-heavy 1,800 with partitions, Mencius 2,160 with FIFO links, SDPaxos 2,160, caps-engaged 100,000 and VR 3,008 with purgatory delays."
 },
